 grows as the program waits. Read twice, half a second apart, without
 stopping the timer.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-32.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   elapsed was read without stopping the timer
   the first read covers the first wait
   elapsed grew while the timer ran
)
a timer called 'job timer'.
Start the 'job timer'.
Wait 200 milliseconds.
a number called 'the early read' is the 'job timer''s elapsed in milliseconds.
Wait 500 milliseconds.
a number called 'the later read' is the 'job timer''s elapsed in milliseconds.
If the 'job timer''s running then, print "elapsed was read without stopping the timer".
Otherwise, print "the timer stopped itself".
If 'the early read' is greater than 199 then, print "the first read covers the first wait".
Otherwise, print "the first read is only {'the early read'} milliseconds".
If 'the later read' is greater than 'the early read' then, print "elapsed grew while the timer ran".
Otherwise, print "elapsed stood still at {'the later read'} milliseconds".
